:: Start {"position":"500,100","size":"100,100"}
Blank, you've finally woken up.

* Choose an option:
[[What are you?]]
[[What.... happened?]]
[[Where... Where am I?]]

:: What are you? {"position":"450,575","size":"100,100"}
My name is Blank. I'm the computer in charge of managing all the spaceship's operations.

[[What.... happened?]]

:: What.... happened? {"position":"175,550","size":"100,100"}
I am... not sure. There was a power outage and I was disconnected from the rest of the OT approximately 25 hours and 12 minutes ago. I attempted rebooting the system to reconnect with the rest of me.

[[And did you succeed?]]

:: And did you succeed? {"position":"100,700","size":"100,100"}
No. The rest of the system was fractured across the ship. From what I can tell, you are the only crewmate left alive. You need to get to the distress beacon and send for help. The findings of this mission cannot be lost.

[[How do I get to the distress beacon]]

:: How do I get to the distress beacon {"position":"625,750","size":"100,100"}
Two ways out of here. First is the main door — straight to the cockpit, exactly where you need to be. Easy access to the distress beacon… but it’s locked.
Second option: the ventilation system. Longer, cramped, and it doesn’t reach the cockpit.
The door only opens from the centralized AI in the control room. Get there, connect me to the main computer, so I can unlock the door and we can call the distress beacon.
Would you like to see a map?

[[Yes]]
[[No]]

:: Yes {"position":"50,925","size":"100,100"}
Drop Spaceship map.

:: No {"position":"250,950","size":"100,100"}
[[How do I get to the distress beacon]]

:: Where... Where am I? {"position":"650,550","size":"100,100"}
You are currently in the living quarters of the Blank in the center of the spaceship.

[[What are you?]]
[[What.... happened?]]
